# GitHub workflows — snake_case inputs

All keys passed to reusable workflows (`with:` and `secrets:`) must use **snake_case**.

```yaml
# Good
with:
  snow_host_url: "http://example.com"
  expected_url: http://example.com:8080
  server_type: cpx12
secrets:
  registry_user: ${{ secrets.GLOBAL_DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
  ssh_public_key: ${{ secrets.SSH_PUBLIC_KEY }}
  snow_github_token: ${{ secrets.SNOW_GITHUB_TOKEN }}
  env_values: |
    KEY=value

# Bad
with:
  snowHostUrl: "..."
  expected-url: "..."
secrets:
  registryUser: ...
  ssh-public-key: ...
```

Single-word keys (`type`, `name`, `tag`, `host`, `provider`, `destroy`) stay lowercase.

Do not use `kebab-case` or `camelCase` for reusable workflow input/secret names.
